<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY" ;
  triage:title "AI.40 M5 UDS one-frame baseline artifact is a failed/degenerate run and run_admission_capacity.py has no validation gate rejecting a non-conforming baseline" ;
  triage:description "Successor to ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-CHRONOLOGY (chronology sub-claim resolved and closed at 1f6b2cbb). The retained pre-AI.39 baseline artifact reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072313.590684-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json (source_revision fb6b26363c5bb0bbb11a6cf167d090385dc53d35, genuinely pre-AI.39) is itself an invalid measurement: sample_count=1 (sprint doc requires minimum 10), run_duration_s=0.138 (sprint doc requires ~20s), passed=false at both interval and run level, first_failure='HTTP 503: sqlite connection budget exceeded (max 3 concurrent reader handles...)', admissions_per_second=180.94 (far below the sprint's own 1,000/s floor). scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py's load_baseline_median() (lines ~613-631) returns the real numeric median computed from this failed run with no validation of the artifact's own passed/sample_count/run_duration_s fields; evaluate_profile_thresholds() (line 592) then consumes that value directly as `baseline_passed = baseline_median is None or median >= baseline_median`, so a degenerate ~181/s floor trivially passes for any subsequent measurement. baseline_reference() (lines ~634-650) separately surfaces a `passed` boolean as descriptive metadata only -- this is NOT the value consumed by the gate, and is not itself a safeguard. Independently confirmed by quality-mgr via direct read of the raw JSON artifact and the three named functions; independently corroborated in full technical detail (same file:line citations, same raw-artifact fields) by both req-qa (filed as ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY) and arch-qa (filed as ARCH-001, RULE-013) during AI40-QA-4. ruthless-boundary-qa's AI40-QA-4 disposition characterized the `passed:false` field as inert/non-gating metadata and called this fixed; that characterization is factually incorrect -- it conflates baseline_reference()'s descriptive `passed` field with load_baseline_median()'s numeric return value, which is what evaluate_profile_thresholds actually gates on. test_baseline_reference_retains_source_revision_and_observed_result in test_run_admission_capacity.py documents that a passed:false baseline payload is accepted and retained unchanged, with no rejection path -- the existing test suite codifies this gap rather than guarding against it." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "follow_up" ;
  triage:category "acceptance-gap" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI40 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py" ;
  triage:line 613 ;
  triage:snippet "STILL OPEN at c73ab129 (AI40-QA-5). load_baseline_median (lines 613-637) now has a real validation gate -- rejects baseline.get('passed', False) is False, sample_count < minimum_sample_count, run_duration_s < target_duration_s -- confirmed present in code by quality-mgr, arch-qa, and req-qa. BUT quality-mgr independently verified the checked-in evidence artifacts contradict this: reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072313.590684-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json is itself a self-failed baseline record (passed=false, sample_count=1, run_duration_s=0.138) -- exactly the shape the new gate is supposed to reject -- and reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072441.255944-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json embeds it as its consumed baseline (matching source_revision/generated_at/run_duration_s) with baseline_median_admissions_per_second=180.94 computed from it, and thresholds.baseline_passed=true / top-level passed=true with no failure recorded. This means either (a) the checked-in evidence is stale, generated by a pre-fix script version and left committed as if authoritative, or (b) the fix does not take effect on the real invocation path -- in both cases the repo's checked-in AI.40 M5 pre-AI.39 baseline evidence is not genuine and the sprint's own acceptance criteria are violated by the currently committed artifacts. Independently confirmed by quality-mgr direct JSON read and corroborated in full technical detail by req-qa (ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY-STILL-OPEN) during AI40-QA-5. NOT closed." ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s40-local-transport-benchmark" ;
  triage:headSha "c73ab129" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/S40/c73ab129> .

